       For the definition of the Gamma function, see ttggaammmmaa(3).

       The  llggaammmmaa(),  llggaammmmaaff(),  and  llggaammmmaall() functions return the natural
       logarithm of the absolute value of the Gamma function.  The sign of the
       Gamma function is returned in the external integer _s_i_g_n_g_a_m declared  in
       _<_m_a_t_h_._h_>.  It is 1 when the Gamma function is positive or zero, -1 when
       it is negative.

       Since  using  a constant location _s_i_g_n_g_a_m is not thread‐safe, the func‐
       tions llggaammmmaa__rr(), llggaammmmaaff__rr(), and llggaammmmaall__rr()  have  been  introduced;
       they return the sign via the argument _s_i_g_n_p.

